{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested for R1 revision 8 at exact a549aac6ef11a5a529c4e341443b1615eb72c069, all four invited artifacts, design only. The adopted revision-7 base remains in force. Four P2 corrections are needed in this candidate.\n\nP2 1 — capacity admission reads transport acknowledgment without replay evidence. Main:4152 counts transport-unacknowledged sends, while 4154–4160 says Used/Reserved derive from history and definition, and 4207 admits new work only when every dimension fits. Main:613–629 permits acknowledgment bookkeeping outside history and forbids judgments depending on other mutable values; 1874–1875/2660–2661 keeps advisory acknowledgments outside authoritative results. Supported witness: the same sealed history has one advisory send, with an outstanding-send budget of one; a new input sends another advisory. Acknowledging the first changes refusal to admission without a new scope entry or retained judgment input. The exhaustive retained-input/checkpoint forms supply no acknowledgment evidence. The budget's trusted numeric value does not remedy missing usage evidence. Define the durable/retained acknowledgment state used by authoritative capacity, or keep transport backpressure outside replay-derived Used. Preserve pending requests and essential settlements; do not erase duties.\n\nP2 2 — settlement byte reservations omit newly retained evidence. Main:4151 counts entries plus retained inputs. The reservation at 4190–4194 covers the settling entry's declared fields, effects and sends plus an envelope allowance, temporarily the 256 KiB entry-size stand-in. A supported handler can settle a waiting item after an each+fact guard checks a list of 32 authentic foreign proof entries, each holding ordinary, non-detached 64 KiB text. Main:1064–1079/1488–1489 permits these forms; 2966–2978 retains their bytes. The handler's own fields contain 32 references and its own state effect, while about 2 MiB of newly retained source bytes is additional Used. That is not covered by its entry-form reservation, contradicting 4206/4220's guarantee that settlement draws only its own reservation and always fits. Compute a finite reservation for the actual maximum newly retained inputs, including foreign sources and capability/outcome evidence, with explicit dedup and byte domains. Leave numerical measurement to R4; correcting only the envelope number or borrowing another duty's reserve does not specify this accounting. No measured runtime overrun is claimed.\n\nP2 3 — automatic issue closure writes an incompatible provenance fact. lane-instantiations.md:156 declares issue.intent.closedBy as fact kinds close-own/close-any/closes under issue. Its closes handler:252 assigns source.ref from the verified sender in change; the publication handler:386 creates that sender entry. Under main:1102–1105/1742–1750 it is a change/publication fact, outside the destination type. An authentic published update to an open issue whose plan condition holds therefore cannot apply the promised closure. Choose one coherent provenance: the issue's local deciding entry, or the foreign publication typed and retained appropriately. Align the slot, assignment, page and replay meaning; preserve generic fact/destination checks. Publication, issue closure and the requester's judgment remain distinct.\n\nP2 4 — the merge eligibility statement lacks each job's deciding result. The companion job:281 has no result reference; check/check-error:333–334 create separate final result items and update job state without linking the deciding result. merge:361 collects only the job's opening fact, name and state. Main:1827–1834 inserts no result implicitly. Adopted R3 at 8b8f946d, main:2412–2413/2582–2593/2980, requires those exact result entries so the destination can qualify the signing key, configuration and result under fresh authority/rules. An opening fact plus stated passed state does not identify the deciding pass. Make the exact first deciding-result evidence mechanically derivable and retained in the complete statement, including requested/timed-out/no-answer and superseded distinctions. An explicitly specified exact-head/prefix evidence path could be an alternative, with its closure, custody, bounds and trust stated. This is incomplete contract evidence, not an observed forged-result acceptance in an unimplemented destination. Planner request 9d55ac57 already owns this and correction 3; keep them in the existing follow-through.\n\nArchitecture: the 78 actual I1 dispositions, typed lane companion, preparation/outcome ownership, retained-input restrictions and essential-settlement accounting advance the complete common contract. Their explicit forms make the four inconsistencies above reviewable; those must be corrected before adoption. All 19 disclosed companion differences and remaining R2/R3/IA/platform definitions, actual bounds, capacities, source admission and joint runtime evidence remain owed. The candidate's A labels are proposed dispositions, not adoption. Do not narrow to a first Jam or let estimates reduce functionality.\n\nSecurity: preserve authenticated source-entry checks, complete job/result/key evidence, per-observation source/time/run/window restrictions, staged-ref snapshot custody, own versus published ancestry and independent reviewer attribution. The four carried security details retain owners; human controller removal/last-key revocation still requires the accepted hosted-work pause policy and exact operational/source implementation. The capacity fixes must not create an unrecorded second authoritative writer or permit essential duties to consume unrelated reservations.\n\nSimplification: use the existing main/matrix/companion and capability boundaries. No additional verifier engine, architecture note, generic field sweep, test quota or heavyweight gate is needed. Keep the private seed/export boundary, bounded queries and compact useful producer witnesses. Nonblocking clarifications: advisory table's zero sends should explicitly constrain generic advisory handler forms; list enumeration can be complete while nested guards are unavailable; successive party-list changes are distinct from mutually exclusive conditional effects. Missing attribution sources already explicitly add nothing in 6.7, so no separate attribution finding is asserted.\n\nExisting editorial/provenance request 687d6524 remains required: reconcile adopted current R0/R2/R3/R4 bases, current R1 commission, actual R4 revision-8 reading and proposed changes. The opening still describes current accepted bases as unreviewed/unadopted. Correct the projection without implying this candidate's adoption or overstating source reading. These corrections are already tracked, not a new source gate.\n\nCoverage: root's prior full adopted R1v7 reading transfers through complete changed-byte review by the static team. The first reviewer fully read current main 1–2725 and 3270–4466, full 295-line matrix including every revision-8 change, and all 395 lines of the new lane companion, comparing all 78 dispositions with fully read fc40 deltas. The second reviewer fully read every changed main hunk through section 9. Root freshly read current 2719–3270, the four findings' complete relevant type/effect/capacity contexts, all exact artifact/invitation statements and the current planner corrections; the retained inventory's identical blob b27b17b6d86559fd18be688c2134b48ad75efe9a transfers its prior full reading. The capacity reviewer independently fully read 5.1,6.6,7.4,9.1–9.3 and17 plus retained-input kind/checkpoint context. This is complete collective static coverage; it is not a claim that every reviewer freshly read all four bodies.\n\nExact SHA-256: main 25670ebdb3dcf227b3b7c2fd438cd5cec500f7b5240b493852fd898beee0b727 (314465 bytes / 4466 LF); matrix 0cdc3bd8bb0b90cc3dfd9736fee4089f4cf2ac4cdb2cdb3144b229f1f28e7c31 (35284 / 295); inventory a2b8f683ff81d48d3136d8a484da1dacc26f858709223c5b2bf6d75a5da7e26f 